  "description": "Certificate of Lawful Existing Development: Conversion of Two flats to single dwellinghouse.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The existing use of the of single dwellinghouse on site is residential (Use Class C3(a)) which was converted from two residential flats which is also under Use Class C3(a) would not result in a material change of use from Use Class C3. Therefore, the existing use of the site would not constitute development as defined by section 55(2)(a)(i) and (f) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) and as defined by Article 3 sub-paragraph (1A) of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes Order) 1987 (as amended). The existing use of the site as a single dwellinghouse is therefore lawful.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
